        </mxCell>

        <!-- Scalability & principles -->
        <mxCell id="notes" value="&lt;b&gt;Two checks, never blended:&lt;/b&gt; (1) Repair-fit: complaint + diagnosis + inspection evidence vs the recommended repair, grounded on similar cases. Verdict is Supported, Potentially excessive, or Insufficient evidence. (2) Price check: catalogue and labour-time guide set the baseline for that same submitted repair; the model estimates the usual paid parts $ and hours and how far the quote sits from them. An engine-block quote is priced as an engine block. A smaller repair is priced from the catalogue only after repair-fit names it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why two NLP paths:&lt;/b&gt; Offline structures closed claims into one JSON schema for the index and the features. Online extracts the new claim with the same schema and flags inconsistencies. The agent decides." style="rounded=1;arcSize=4;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fontSize=11;fillColor=#FFFDE7;strokeColor=#F9AB00;" vertex="1" parent="1">
